# SE quality constitution

Hard invariants for every change. Details live in linked SoTs — do not weaken gates.

## Deterministic gates (never soften)

- Whole-repo coverage floor **98.7%** (`fail_under`); CI cov cell **3.11 only**
- **complexipy ≤5**; file **LOC ≤225** (src and tests when ratchet applies); cohesion over `part2` chops
- **No `utils/` grab-bag** — concept-named modules (`doc_engine.core.*`, domain packages)
- Descriptive names only — refuse single-letter mode/flags (`m`/`o`/`c`)
- Prefer structural search for citation claims; follow `CLAUDE.md` / claims checker

## SoT vs derived (DDIA)

- Authoritative metrics (oracle `coverage.xml`, fail_under, size, complexipy, claims) are **boolean SoT**
- Climb Cover%, gap-average, LLM-as-judge, Recall@K are **sensors** — never silent merge proof
- Scoped `--cov` + fail_under ≠ whole-repo 98.7 — never conflate
- Policy **16-A**: climb artifacts use a **distinct** path (e.g. `coverage.climb.xml`); only `coverage.xml` is oracle SoR
- No fuzzy/PID “confidence of green”; no cross-worktree `coverage combine`

## Process (SDD)

- **Spec → Implement → Verify → Archive**; one active tip writer; no force-push tip thrash
- Prefer strategies/ports (OCP) over if/elif gods; vertical/concept slices (DDD)
- Refuse by default: in-tree Rust (unless profiled), PIT operator zoo, ECS/mesh/Backstage theater
- Path/task scoping SoT = Project Rules **MDC globs** — do **not** add nested `AGENTS.md` as a second path SoT

